    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with significant upside, spearheaded by **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12) and **Christian Yelich** (73.17). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our top play; his favorable matchup against Feltner, combined with an elite leadoff spot and a 14% boost from dynamic platoon metrics, makes him a primary target for stolen base production. Similarly, **Christian Yelich** benefits from a soft matchup against Cecconi and a rare 100% stolen base projection due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, locking him into a high-ceiling role. **Kyle Schwarber** (68.20) and **Yordan Alvarez** (63.90) remain core building blocks despite the latter facing a tough southpaw in Valdez; **Yordan Alvarez**\u2019s elite 0.452 xwOBA effectively overrides the platoon disadvantage, ensuring he stays in the lineup to anchor our power categories.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Lars Nootbaar** (57.09), who fell just shy of the lineup threshold. While **Lars Nootbaar** possessed a strong dynamic platoon edge against King, his lower baseline projection relative to our starting outfielders kept him on the pine in favor of the more efficient **Carson Benge** (63.08). We are also monitoring the status of several players currently marked \"Lineup Pending,\" most notably **Gary Sanchez**, **Junior Caminero**, **Luke Raley**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Christian Yelich**, and **Carson Benge**. If these official lineups shift lower in the batting order, their efficiency scores will see immediate downward revisions. Finally, caution is advised for **Chase Meidroth**, who draws a difficult assignment against Gerrit Cole; while his 53.91 score is viable, the high caliber of the opposing arm represents the most significant risk to our daily production.",
